# streetlevel itself is in requirements-nodeps.txt and is installed with --no-deps (#237): it declares
# pyequilib, whose 0.6.0 requires torch, and a normal resolve puts torch, triton and sixteen nvidia-*/cuda-*
# wheels (several GB) into a venv where no production module imports any of them. pip has no per-requirement
# --no-deps, so the requirements streetlevel really needs are listed here instead. The five below, with
# aiohttp, requests, numpy and Pillow above, are everything `from streetlevel import streetview` imports,
# measured on Python 3.10 against streetlevel 0.12.11 (reports/2026-11-15-streetlevel-no-deps.md). They carry
# no floor because streetlevel declares none; constraints.txt holds the versions that were tested. Declared by
# streetlevel but never imported on that path, and so NOT installed: pyequilib, protobuf, pyfrpc,
# pycryptodome, cython, pytest, pytest-asyncio. tests/test_streetlevel_api.py fails when streetlevel's
# declared list stops matching these two lists, which is the cue to measure again.
pyproj
scipy
bd09convertor
CoordinatesConverter
pyexiv2
